<h1>SetView</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Changes the current viewpoint.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Parameters</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><i style="font-style:italic;">RotX</i></b>, <b><i>RotY</i></b>, <b><i>RotZ</i></b>, <b><i>TrX</i></b>, <b><i>TrY</i></b>, <b><i>TrZ</i></b>, <b><i>MinX</i></b>, <b><i>MinY</i></b>, <b><i>MinZ</i></b>, <b><i>MaxX</i></b>, <b><i>MaxY</i></b>, <b><i>MaxZ</i></b>, <b><i>FMinX</i></b>, <b><i>FMinY</i></b>, <b><i>FMinZ</i></b>, <b><i>FMaxX</i></b>, <b><i>FMaxY</i></b>, and <b><i>FmaxZ</i></b> – formal parameters describing the state of the matrices that define the viewport.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Example:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode" style="font-family:Courier New;">SetView( RotX=-0.318748, RotY=0.205917, RotZ=-0.033976, TrX=-53.154134, TrY=-79.625520, TrZ=15.354748, MinX=-388.616911, MinY=-329.761854, MinZ=-5165.054932, MaxX=163.432345, MaxY=222.287402, MaxZ=5681.560425, FMinX=-276.024628, FMinY=-276.024628, FMinZ=-5165.054932, FMaxX=276.024628, FMaxY=276.024628, FMaxZ=5681.560425 )</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">&#160;</p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span>: This command is generated when executing viewport operations using mouse, slider or shortcuts. The following operations output SetView command:<br>
- rotate;<br>
- pan;<br>
- zoom all;<br>
- zoom in;<br>
- zoom out<br>
- zoom selected<br>
SetView is a complicate command and should not be directly typed by the user.</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
